        "solution": "Check the VIN with Ford or NHTSA. Dealers replace the oil-pump tensioner assembly and oil-pump drive belt free of charge. If engine failure occurred because of a damaged belt or tensioner, Ford authorized free engine replacement. The recall does not establish rattling, knocking, squealing, a no-restart condition, or generic oil-pressure fault codes as universal warnings.",
